[i][DEMO GIF SLOT — pawn swaps its rifle for the excellent copy][/i]

Quality control for [b]Combat Extended[/b] loadouts — the same filters vanilla outfit policies have always had, plus automatic weapon upgrades.

[h1]What it does[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Per-loadout quality & hit-point floors.[/b] Set a quality range and an HP range on any CE loadout (right in the loadout dialog, with the widgets you know from outfit policies). Fetching skips items outside the ranges, and a carried weapon below the floor is dropped and replaced — exactly how apparel outside an outfit filter behaves. Ranges default wide open: the mod does nothing until you narrow them.
[*][b]Auto weapon upgrade[/b] [i](toggleable, on by default)[/i]. Pawns swap loadout weapons for a strictly higher-quality copy of the [b]same weapon and same material[/b] when one is available. Rides CE's own loadout schedule (and the Assign tab's update-now button) — no extra scanning. The replaced weapon drops in place, unforbidden, for your haulers.
[/list]

[h1]Requires[/h1]
Harmony and Combat Extended. Works fine alongside Simple Sidearms and the [url=https://github.com/eebette/CombatExtended-SimpleSidearms-Compatibility-Patch]CE+SS compatibility suite[/url] (upgrades inform Simple Sidearms' memory automatically), but needs neither.

[h1]Good to know[/h1]
[list]
[*]Safe to add mid-save. Removing mid-save leaves a one-time load warning and nothing else.
[*]A floor with no allowed instance available means the pawn goes without — same as outfit filters. Widen the range or craft better gear.
[*]Weapons-only by design: meals, medicine, and ammo in loadouts are never quality/HP-gated (HP-gating consumables would silently starve pawns).
[/list]

[h1]Links & credit[/h1]
Source, issues, docs: [url=https://github.com/eebette/Loadout-Quality-for-Combat-Extended]GitHub[/url]. MIT-licensed.
